==============================================================================
(1) STAGE 1 — THE MODES START DEGENERATE
==============================================================================
  With only the medium bond on (b = 0), eps_q = a for every q:
          mode   lambda_q     eps_q       w_q
  ------------------------------------------
     neutral        0.0   1.00000   1.00000
     charged        3.0   1.00000   1.00000
     charged        3.0   1.00000   1.00000

  Exactly degenerate — the medium bond is blind to which face it holds. So a common
  occupation number across the three modes is not an assumption at this stage; it is
  what any equilibrium or common preparation gives when the frequencies coincide.

==============================================================================
(2) STAGE 2 — RAMP THE FACE-FACE BONDS AND WATCH THE ACTION
==============================================================================
  Each mode is integrated through the ramp with velocity-Verlet, starting from a common
  action J = 1. If the action is the invariant, every mode ends at J = 1 whatever its
  frequency did.

  ramp duration = 1256.6 = 400 charged-mode periods (adiabatic)

        mode   w_initial    w_final   J_initial     J_final      drift
  --------------------------------------------------------------------
     neutral     1.00000    1.00000    1.000000    0.999969    0.0031%
     charged     1.00000    2.00000    1.000000    0.999992    0.0008%

  The charged mode's frequency doubles and its action does not move. That is adiabatic
  invariance, computed rather than quoted.

==============================================================================
(3) THE CONTROL — A FAST RAMP MUST BREAK IT
==============================================================================
  A check that cannot fail is not a check. If the action were conserved for ANY ramp the
  result would be trivial, so the sudden limit has to break it.

     ramp (charged-mode periods)   J_final (charged)      drift
  --------------------------------------------------------------
                            0.02            1.997675    99.767%
                            0.20            1.787396    78.740%
                            2.00            0.939182     6.082%
                           20.00            0.999992     0.001%
                          200.00            0.999992     0.001%

  It breaks in the sudden limit and converges in the slow one, monotonically. So the
  invariance is doing real work here, and the premise it replaces is ADIABATICITY --
  a statement about the assembly rate, not about occupation numbers.

==============================================================================
(4) WHAT THE RAMP DELIVERS AT THE END
==============================================================================
    <x^2> neutral (from the integration) = 0.99992707
    <x^2> charged (from the integration) = 0.50004484
    ratio                                 = 0.50008131   (expect w_0/w_1 = 1/2)

    R^2/f_0^2 = 2 x ratio = 1.00016262   (the null needs 1)
    Q = (1 + R^2/f_0^2)/3 = 0.66672087   (2/3 = 0.66666667)
    miss = 81.3 ppm  (integration error, not physics)

  The null comes out of the integrated dynamics, not out of the premise it was used to
  justify. The residual is claimed to be numerical, so it has to be shown to converge:

    steps/period              Q   ppm from 2/3  ratio to previous
  ----------------------------------------------------------------
             100    0.666868243         302.36                 --
             200    0.666774421         161.63               1.87
             400    0.666720873          81.31               1.99
             800    0.666693695          40.54               2.01

  The error falls with the timestep, so it is the integrator and not the physics. The
  exact statement remains the algebraic one: <x^2> ~ J/w with J common gives R = f_0.

==============================================================================
(5) WHAT (P4) HAS BECOME
==============================================================================
  BEFORE: 'the modes carry equal quanta' — a postulate about occupation numbers, with
  nothing behind it, carrying the whole derivation of Q = 2/3.

  AFTER: two physical statements, both attackable:
    (P4a) ASSEMBLY ORDER — the medium bond precedes the face-face bonds, because a face
          is an excitation of the condensate. At that stage the three modes are exactly
          degenerate, so equal occupation is automatic rather than assumed.
    (P4b) ADIABATICITY — the face-face bonds turn on slowly compared with the mode
          frequencies, so each mode conserves its action through the splitting.

  This is a real reduction and not a rename: (P4a) is a claim about what the faces ARE,
  and (P4b) is a claim about a rate, and both can be checked against the corpus's own
  freeze dynamics. Neither is a statement about quantum numbers.

  WHAT IS STILL OWED. The corpus must supply the ramp rate at freeze and confirm it is
  slow against w ~ 39 keV. That is the same fork the delivery-law discriminator opened —
  the freeze's timescale — now demanded from the other side. One number closes both.
